The number of words is certainly helpful, but isn't the whole story.
As Robin points out, there would be a lot of emotives and things in
Lojban which are not usually written in English, as they're largely
associated with intonation. So, the Lojban might be longer, but it
likely carries more information about speaker attitude and such than
the English. Which is to say, it (probably) has higher information
density.

Chris

